  "text": "WHO Guideline on Self-Care Interventions for Health and Well-Being | Publisher: World Heal\nChapter 4: Integrative Health & Self-Care Governance\nIntegrative health traditions, including traditional lifestyle practices,\nshould be evaluated against safety principles. Guidelines for Traditional\nLifestyle Practices: 1. Lifestyle & Rest: Traditional practices focusing\non warm water hydration, mindful breathing, and structured sleep alignment\nare supported for general wellness. 2. Safety Disclaimers: Traditional\nlifestyle practices are non-pharmacological educational options and should\nnever replace emergency medical care. 3. Quality Control: Avoid unverified\ncommercial oral mixtures or unregulated compounds.\nPage 4 of 4 | Official Educational Resource",
